      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-03T16:20:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: I think it\u0027s clearer to log the result of the Flash size in the code that calls this function. Something like:\n\nif (read_flash_size_register(\u0026flash_size)) {\n  printf(\"Flash size\");\n  chip-\u003eflash_size \u003d flash_size;\n} else {\n  printf(stderr, \"Failed to read the size of the Flash, assuming default %u bytes\\n\");\n}\n\n\nThat way the calling code does not depend on the implementation of the read_a_register function, only on the usual API contract. It\u0027s unusual that read_a_register functions also print the result to stdout, they usually read the value of the register and let the calling code decide what to do with it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1021,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1021,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "8586d7d6838e7acbf5e95eaf9faf7532729f1add",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
